  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 25-layer SiO2/Al2O3 multi-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layers 1-25 alternate SiO2/Al2O3 starting with SiO2. Fix layers 12, 13, and 14 at exactly 67.5 nm thickness (non-optimizable). Optimize layers 1-11 and 15-25 with bounds ±15% around quarter-wave thickness at 267.5 nm center wavelength (SiO2 ~45 nm, Al2O3 ~67 nm). Apply optimization cost penalty of 0.01 per pair of consecutive layers with thickness similarity >95%. Wavelength bands: maximize transmittance 255-280 nm, minimize transmittance 300-700 nm, minimize transmittance 700-1100 nm. Total layer count exactly 25 finite coating layers. No metal layers. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with diversity constraint. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 255–280 nm; low transmittance in 300–700 nm; low transmittance in 700–1100 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 300–700 nm; transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30; no metal layers; conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials only.",
